    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-060 — Eliminate string-copy overhead in layout hot path.** One commit. **Docs follow after merge.**\n\nTargets the 25.13% `fill_sides` lambda and ~9.5% allocation churn from the perf profile. **12.0% layout win measured (median-of-3).**\n\n## The verified delta (Release, median-of-3 Wikipedia)\n\n| Run | Layout |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | 2476.3ms |\n| 2 | 2328.2ms |\n| 3 | 2356.6ms |\n| **Median** | **2356.6ms** |\n\n**Pre-ADR-060 baseline: 2678ms** (median of 2678/2463/3249)\n\n**2356.6ms = 12.0% win, 321ms saved per Wikipedia page load.** Target was <2420ms; measured comfortably inside. Two of three post runs clustered at 2328-2356 — structural, not variance.\n\nCascade unchanged at ~200ms as expected (no cascade code touched).\n\n## Session-wide perf progression\n\n| Stage | Total | Layout |\n|---|---|---|\n| ADR-058 baseline (before perf work) | 3437ms | 2379ms |\n| ADR-059 (cascade index) | 2950ms | 2750ms* |\n| **ADR-060 (this PR, layout copies)** | **~2555ms** | **2357ms** |\n| **Combined ADR-059+060** | **25.5% win** | — |\n\n*ADR-059's layout measurement was in the 3× variance window; ADR-060's median is more reliable.\n\n## What ships\n\n### `cascade.hpp` / `cascade.cpp`\n\n- **`StringHash` / `StringEq`** with `is_transparent` — enables heterogeneous lookup (string_view key without allocation)\n- **Map type change**: `unordered_map<string, CascadeValue, StringHash, StringEq>` (was default hash/equal)\n- **`ComputedStyle::get_view(string_view)`** → `optional<string_view>` — read-only, no copy\n- **`get()` unchanged** — existing callers keep working\n\n### `layout.cpp`\n\n`fill_sides` inline lambda rewritten:\n\n```cpp\n// Before: 2 allocs per call (key + value copy)\nauto px = [&](const char* p) {\n    const auto v = style->get(p);\n    return v ? parse_length(*v, ctx) : 0.0f;\n};\n\n// After: zero allocs (transparent hash + reference access)\nauto px = [&](std::string_view p) -> float {\n    auto it = style->declarations.find(p);\n    if (it == style->declarations.end()) return 0.0f;\n    return parse_length(it->second.value, ctx);\n};\n```\n\n**3 call sites** (margin / border / padding) inherit the fix from the shared lambda.\n\n### `tests/test_stylesheet.cpp`\n\n- Added `#include \"renderer/css/cascade.hpp\"` (ComputedStyle/CascadeValue live there)\n- 3 new tests: `get_view` return value, nullopt for missing, `const char*` literal (no key alloc)\n\n## Design decisions\n\n**`get_view()` is additive, not replacing `get()`** — some callers need owned strings (`value_or` patterns). Blast radius = only hot-path callers switch.\n\n**Transparent hash is universal** — every `get_view(string_view)` site benefits without per-callsite static keys. Alternative (static const strings in `fill_sides`) would fix one caller but not others.\n\n**Typed `ComputedStyle` fields (the bigger fix) → ADR-061** — ~200 lines, changes data model, touches cascade population. Ship ADR-060's incremental win first to prove methodology.\n\n## What the fix does NOT eliminate\n\n- **`unordered_map::find` hash + compare** — still happens per lookup\n- **`parse_length` string parsing** — still happens per property\n- **`get()` for callers that need owned strings** — correct, they need the copy\n\n**That's why the win is 12%, not 25%.** The remaining ~10-13% requires typed fields (ADR-061 candidate).\n\n## Two implementation bugs caught before shipping\n\n1. **Missing `#include \"renderer/css/cascade.hpp\"`** in test file — `ComputedStyle` / `CascadeValue` live in cascade.hpp, not stylesheet.hpp (which was the only included CSS header).\n2. **Heredoc literal `\\n`** — same Python `'\\\\n'` bug as ADR-059. Appended `\\` + `n` chars to end of test file instead of newline. Fixed via strip + real `\\n`.\n\n**Same three-for-three pattern**: ADR-057 (definition body), ADR-058 (`ctx` scope), ADR-059 (namespace scope), ADR-060 (include + literal newline). **The compiler catches all of these immediately — but only if the whole project is rebuilt AND tests run against the rebuilt binary.**\n\n## Test count\n\n- 680 → 683 cases (+3)\n- 2608 → 2614 assertions (+6)\n- Zero existing test regressions\n\n## Deferred (documented)\n\n- **Typed `ComputedStyle` fields** → ADR-061 (~25% potential, bigger change)\n- **`contains_word` optimization** → cascade-side, ADR-061/062\n- **`parse_length` fast path** → not in top-10 profile\n- **`pthread_rwlock` (4.82%)** → library-internal (GTK/glib/fontconfig), not actionable\n- **`FcCharSetIsSubset` (1.49%)** → fontconfig\n\nRefs #261\n",
